  "operation": {
    "summary": "Delete Credit Notes",
    "deprecated": false,
    "description": "MUTATING operation. Verify target and authorized intent; reconcile outcome before retry. Deletes a credit note identified by the `id` path parameter.\n\nRequires permission to delete invoices/credit notes (a non-owner may delete only credit notes they created unless they hold the delete-all permission). One credit note is deleted per call.\n\nA credit note **cannot be deleted** while it is blocked by a business rule — for example it belongs to a closed POS session, has an approved requisition, has linked documents, or has been submitted to a tax authority; these are rejected with HTTP `401` (see the response below). On success the response is `200` with a confirmation message.",
    "tags": [
      "Endpoints/Sales /Credit Notes",
      "Credit Notes"
    ],
